{
    "name": "E2E YouTube - New Video trigger (self-provoked)",
    "description": "NewVideo listens for PubSubHubbub notifications. The flow provokes one itself: utils.http.Post sends a synthetic Atom feed entry to the connector's own callback route (the one the trigger registers at the hub), the plugin parses it with fast-xml-parser and triggers the component. Needs no YouTube account.",
    "notes": {
        "de630fca-c554-41a3-ba28-8ddcd175d5fe": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 272,
            "width": 832,
            "height": 208,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Self-provoked trigger\n\n`NewVideo.start()` still subscribes the real channel at `pubsubhubbub.appspot.com`, but a real upload is not what this flow waits for. The `Post` component builds the plugin callback URL from its own webhook URL (`g_webhookUrl` → `/plugins/appmixer/google/youtube/trigger/<flowId>/component/<triggerId>`) and POSTs a synthetic Atom entry with `yt:videoId` = `e2eVideo0001`. The route in `routes.js` parses the XML and calls `triggerComponent`, so the whole production receive path runs.\n\nThe `Condition` drops any real notification for the channel that may arrive during the run, so only the synthetic entry reaches the `Assert`."
        }
    },
    "flow": {
